    "size": 20911023,
    "mandatory": false,
    "changelog": "v1.0.2\n\nFixed\n- 32-bit (armeabi-v7a) rootless boot: the published rootfs-armv7.imgz was a bare Debian rootfs missing the Stryker guest provisioning, so the VM stalled 90s on \"Expecting device dev-ttyAMA0.device\" and the agent never came up. The armv7 image is now provisioned like arm64: systemd-udevd (device units resolve), systemd-networkd DHCP (agent ports 1050-1052 reachable), stryker-agentd/stryker-ptyd + stryker-agent.service, and a serial-getty@ttyAMA0 autologin root console.\n- armv7 VM RAM is now capped at 3072 MB: -M virt,highmem=off cannot address more than 3 GB in 32-bit mode, so QEMU refused to launch on devices where the effective RAM exceeded the limit.\n\nAdded\n- scripts/patch-armv7-rootfs.sh: reproducible patch that provisions a bare armv7 rootfs from the repo's own stryker-guest-core.tar asset."
  },
  "news": [
    {
      "id": 2,
      "title": "Stryker 6.0 — Rootless engine & Debian",
      "description": "The full toolset now runs without root: Stryker boots an arm64 QEMU virtual machine and routes tools into the guest. The chroot moved from Alpine to Debian trixie, the same rootfs the VM boots. Also new: a root-free network scanner (mDNS, SSDP, NetBIOS, SNMP), Cameradar RTSP discovery, a reworked dashboard and VM settings. RouterScan has been removed. arm64-v8a only.",
